  "notes": "The named Don highway crossing has two three-lane carriageways, outer sidewalks, continuous box girders, paired concrete pier shafts, red-brown perimeter rails and hooked streetlights. It joins the two mapped elevated viaducts and runs parallel to the separate railway lift bridge. The model covers the approximately 462 m named highway crossing and short connections to the elevated viaducts. The continuing viaducts and ramps remain native viewer geometry. The four mapped carriageway and sidewalk lines and both Don banks fix the horizontal fit. The deck profile, pier shapes, spacing and heights are photo-based visualization estimates. The adjacent steel railway lift bridge is a separate mapped crossing. It remains in the renderer as an independent railway feature.",
